			"text":"CLAUDE",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":0,
			"y":600,
			"width":250,
			"height":60,
			"color":"5"
		},
		{
			"id":"r6e5f60718291b22",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# MCP Roots\n\nRoots are a **permission + file-discovery** mechanism: the client tells the server which directories/URIs it's allowed to touch. Without roots the server can't search the filesystem to resolve a bare filename like \"biking.mp4\" into a full path — it asks the client for approved roots, searches inside them, then calls the real tool with the resolved path.",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-800,
			"y":-320,
			"width":2650,
			"height":180
		},
		{
			"id":"r7f60718291b2c33",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"*Server, internally:*\n\nis_path_allowed() — check the resolved path falls inside an approved root. The SDK doesn't enforce this automatically, server code must validate it.",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":800,
			"y":250,
			"width":340,
			"height":160,
			"color":"3"
		},
		{
			"id":"r80718291b2c3d44",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**Why roots matter**\nUser-friendly (no full paths needed), faster search (scoped to approved dirs), and a security boundary against unauthorized file access.",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-200,
			"y":800,
			"width":1600,
			"height":160,
			"color":"3"
		}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"r918291b2c3d4e55","fromNode":"r1u5e60718291a99","fromSide":"right","toNode":"r2b2c3d4e5f60809","toSide":"left","label":"1 Convert biking.mp4 to mov"},
